      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's generally not recommended to mix diazepam with alcohol, even in small amounts, because both are central nervous system depressants and can intensify each other's effects. This can lead to increased drowsiness, impaired coordination, and potentially dangerous respiratory depression. The risk is particularly high if you're taking a higher dose or have other health conditions. It's best to avoid alcohol while on diazepam to ensure your safety and well-being.",
